HP's Contacts (com.palm.app.contacts), as modernized by webOS Archive for webOS Community
Edition: version 3.2.0, from the webOS CE project's tree (com.palm.app.contacts_3.2.0_all.ipk).
It opens on contacts kept on the device ("On This Device") instead of asking people to get
started with an HP webOS account.

The app was released by LG Electronics under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE); the 3.2.0
changes are webOS Archive's, among them Import vCards in the App Menu (webos-doctor-ce commits
7bd5641, c8b69b6; the tree stays at 3.2.0, so look for app/utils/VCardBatchImport.js).

The app's files are here as the package carries them, with one exception codepoet approved
(rule 5 in CLAUDE.md, 2026-11-02): the layout for a card under 600 px wide, marked [Lunacy] in
app/SplitPane.js, app/Details.js, app/ContactsApp.js and css/contacts.css. It doesn't change
the TouchPad or a tablet, and it has to be carried over when CE's tree is taken again. Any
other change Lunacy needs in the app is made in the webOS CE project and comes here with its
next release.
